It is the remnant of some even older part of the city, as best I can tell.	依我看，這是這座城市更古老一部分的遺跡。
It is of colored glass through which you can see nothing.	這是彩色玻璃，你什麼也看不透。
They look like ordinary bushes of some Eastern variety.	這些看起來像是某種東方常見的普通灌木。
Over the door are two symbols, a crescent moon and a star.	門上方有兩個符號：一彎新月與一顆星。
The crescent and star are both symbols associated with the Goddess.	新月與星辰都是與女神相關的符號。
Bits of plaster have fallen away revealing bricks underneath, a common enough sight in Jerusalem.	部分灰泥已經剝落，露出底下的磚塊，這在耶路撒冷是常見的景象。
The tiles are beautifully decorated, but of no consequence to you.	這些磁磚裝飾精美，但與你無關緊要。
It is a heavy wooden door framed by beautifully glazed tiles.	這是一扇厚重的木門，四周鑲著裝飾精美的釉磚。
She is nowhere in sight, if she is around here at all.	就算她在附近，此刻也不見蹤影。
I see no-one here with whom to speak.	此處不見任何可交談之人。
It is already open.	它已經是開著的。
Such poetic language will never get you through this door.	這般詩意的言語，斷不能讓你通過此門。
A powerful enchantment keeps this door shut. It will not open unless the owner is ready to open it.	一道強大的咒法將此門封鎖。除非主人有意開啟，否則此門絕不會開。
Ahem...it IS closed.	呃……它確實是關著的。
First, you must confront her. Then we shall see what will be.	你得先與她正面相對，之後才知分曉。
You are alone in a hostile city. Do try to avoid rash and foolish actions.	你孤身一人置身於敵意四伏的城中，切莫輕舉妄動。
There is no merchant here.	此處並無商販。
It is too high.	太高了。
Enter. Then we shall speak.	進來吧，我們再談。
I will not tolerate such filth.	這等污穢之語，我絕不容忍。
I warned you once. Now you will never step across my threshold.	我警告過你一次。如今，你休想再跨過我的門檻。
Enter, if you would speak with me.	若想與我交談，便進來吧。
What are you waiting for, Arthur? It is open.	你還在等什麼，亞瑟？門開著呢。
There is no need. Fatima controls this door.	沒有這個必要，這扇門由法提瑪掌控。
There is no answer.	沒有回應。
Fatima has finished with you. She will not answer.	法提瑪已經與你了結，她不會再回應了。
You were warned. This door will never open for you again.	你已被警告過。這扇門再也不會為你開啟。
Enter.	進來。
You may try, but I do not think you will succeed.	你儘管一試，但我不認為你會成功。
I really think you are better off keeping your eyes on Fatima.	我認為你最好把目光放在法提瑪身上。
This is no girl, Arthur!	這可不是個尋常女子，亞瑟！
I can tell you nothing.	我什麼也不能告訴你。
Above you is an unadorned ceiling.	你頭頂上是一片素淨無飾的天花板。
Fatima awaits you upon the other side of a tiled pool. Water splashes from a bronze dolphin fountain. At the other end is a couch amply decorated with pillows. There is only one other door from the room.	法提瑪在磁磚砌成的水池另一端等著你。青銅海豚噴泉濺灑著水花，池的另一端擺著一張堆滿抱枕的長榻。這房間只有另一扇門可通行。
Nothing has changed, except perhaps your level of caution.	一切如舊，變的或許只有你的戒心。
There is no bench, but there is a couch.	這裡沒有長椅，但有一張長榻。
There is the front door, through which you entered, and a side door which seems to be the only other exit.	這裡有你進來時走的前門，以及一扇側門，看來是唯一的另一個出口。
That is the front door, through which you entered.	那是你進來時走的前門。
That side door is the only other door in this room besides the front door.	除了前門，那扇側門是這房間裡唯一的另一扇門。
It is a piece of dark slate with a painted edge.	這是一塊深色石板，邊緣繪有彩紋。
The crescent over the side door is a lunar symbol associated with the Goddess.	側門上方的新月，是與女神相關的月亮符號。
It is a beautifully sculpted bronze dolphin.	這是一尊雕工精美的青銅海豚。
I do not recognize her plants, but I doubt they are important.	我認不出她種的這些植物，但我想它們並不重要。
The utterly clear water ripples in a most mesmerizing way.	這池澄澈見底的水，泛起令人目眩神迷的漣漪。
The couch with its wealth of lush pillows suggests the pursuit of physical pleasures.	這張長榻堆滿了華美的抱枕，透著追求肉體歡愉的意味。
Everything in this room, including Fatima, should be considered a possible trap.	這房間裡的一切，包括法提瑪在內，都該視為可能的陷阱。
Aye, you had best avoid it unless you have reason to think it is safe.	正是，除非你有理由相信它是安全的，否則最好避開。
It is paved with squares of terra cotta.	地面鋪著一塊塊赤陶磚。
The room has no windows. The alcoves are filled with tiles glazed with complex Arabian patterns.	這房間沒有窗戶，壁龕裡鑲滿了繪有繁複阿拉伯紋樣的釉磚。
The walls have arches and recessed tiled alcoves.	牆上有拱門，以及嵌入牆內、鋪著磁磚的壁龕。
The alcoves look primarily decorative, covered with brightly glazed, patterned tiles.	這些壁龕看來主要作裝飾之用，覆滿色澤鮮亮、紋樣繁複的釉磚。
The glazed tiles are bright and dazzle the eye.	這些釉磚色澤鮮豔，令人目眩。
Really, Arthur, that would be most unwise here.	說真的，亞瑟，在此處這麼做極不明智。
It is good that you have returned for you have yet to pass the Test of Symbols.	你能回來是件好事，畢竟你尚未通過符號考驗。
Welcome back, seeker. You have learned a difficult lesson. There is but one way to walk through my outer door in safety and that is when I will it.	歡迎歸來，求道者。你已學到了艱難的一課。要安然走過我的外門，唯有一法——待我有意讓你通過之時。
She is so exquisite, that even I am moved by her beauty. And she is no ordinary woman. I feel a power here that rivals my own.	她如此絕美，連我也為之動容。她絕非尋常女子，我在此處感受到一股足以與我匹敵的力量。
You have earned the right to question me.  Ask of me what you will.	你已贏得向我提問的資格。有話儘管問。
When I want something of you, seeker, I will ask it.	求道者，若我有所求於你，自會開口。
I care not what amount of coin you have. I ask for the entire purse, be it empty or full, for the purse represents attachment to material wealth.	你錢囊裡有多少錢，我並不在意。我要的是整個錢囊，無論空滿，因為錢囊象徵著對物質財富的執著。
What I have to offer you is greater than any sum of money.	我所能給你的，遠勝過任何一筆錢財。
Your lips will not reach that far.  And I do NOT advise getting closer.	你的嘴唇夠不著那麼遠。我也奉勸你別再靠近。
By refusing my seductions, you have proven yourself to be a man of moral worth. But beware that you do not undo it all with a passing moment of weakness.	拒絕我的誘惑，證明了你是個有德之人。但要當心，莫讓一時的軟弱，毀了這一切。
You would look like a fool.	你這樣看起來會像個傻子。
For that, you must find the hierophant.	為此，你必須找到祭司。
I cannot see what good that would do you.	我看不出這對你有什麼好處。
There is no key to be gotten.	沒有鑰匙可拿。
There is but one way out, through the front door.	只有一條出路，經由前門。
Would you expect anyone to answer?	你以為會有人回應嗎？
You may leave by the front door at any time, though I advise you not to do so unless I give you my blessing. The inner door opens only at my command.	你隨時可從前門離去，不過我勸你除非得到我的祝福，否則莫要如此。內門唯有依我之命方能開啟。
You may leave by the front door at any time, though I advise you not to do so unless I give you my blessing. The inner door is open. The Test awaits you.	你隨時可從前門離去，不過我勸你除非得到我的祝福，否則莫要如此。內門已經開啟，考驗正等著你。
It is good that you have brought this. Keep it close to you.	你能帶著這個來是件好事，將它貼身留著。
I should think you have had more than your share of merchants this day.	我想你今日打交道的商販已經夠多了。
No, do not eat it now. You may have need for it later.	不，現在別吃它，日後或許用得著。
My sacred waters are protected by a spell to keep them clean of any defilement, though I will allow you to drink of it.	我這聖水受一道咒法守護，不受任何污染，但我允許你飲用。
My sacred waters are not for such mundane uses.	我這聖水，不作這等世俗用途。
Fatima's heady perfume and musky incense overwhelms your senses with sensual pleasure.	法提瑪馥郁的香氣與濃烈的麝香薰香，讓你的感官沉浸在肉慾的愉悅之中。
You cannot draw your sword and if you turn to violence against me, I will punish you.	你拔不出劍。若你對我動用武力，我必懲罰你。
You are far from the enchantress who gave you this sword and my power is supreme here. Your sword will not leave its scabbard in my presence.	賜你這把劍的女法師遠在天邊，此地是我的力量至高無上。在我面前，你的劍絕不會出鞘。
Do not seek to lose the good favor you have won from me.	莫要親手斷送你在我這裡贏得的恩寵。
Soon enough, my handsome one.	快了，我的美男子。
Knowledge must be earned before it will be given.	知識須先贏得，方能授予。
You have passed my Test and are truly you are the most worthy of all men who have passed my door. Go with my blessings and find the hierophant.	你已通過我的考驗，確實是所有踏過我門檻的人之中最堪當之人。帶著我的祝福去吧，找到祭司。
Enter the door and take my test.	進門，接受我的考驗。
You are acquainted with my front door.  This inner door leads to my Test of Symbols.	我的前門你已熟悉。這扇內門通往我的符號考驗。
If you persevere, you will find the Grail.  Now, you must seek out the hierophant and gain entrance to the catacombs, as did Galahad before you.	若你堅持到底，終將尋得聖杯。如今，你必須尋出祭司，設法進入地下墓窖，如同在你之前的葛拉漢一般。
You have trials of body, spirit and heart yet to face if you are to wrest the Cup of Regeneration from the Goddess and take it with you as the Grail.	若要從女神手中奪得重生之杯、將它當作聖杯帶走，你還有肉身、心靈與意志的試煉要面對。
From here, your path must lie through the deadly catacombs, as it did for the man who came here before you, the one called Galahad.	從此處起，你的路必須穿過那致命的地下墓窖，正如在你之前來到此地、名叫葛拉漢的那人一樣。
But to walk safely in the catacombs, you must pass my Test of Symbols.	但要在地下墓窖中安然而行，你必須先通過我的符號考驗。
He, too, resisted my seductions. I have learned from the hierophant that Galahad entered the catacombs to continue his search.	他也曾抵擋住我的誘惑。我從祭司那裡得知，葛拉漢已進入地下墓窖，繼續他的尋索。
But he did not pass the Test of Symbols that I placed before him, and so I fear he has suffered by entering the catacombs without the gift of the hierophant.	但他未能通過我為他設下的符號考驗，因此我擔心，他未帶祭司的贈禮便進入墓窖，恐已遭逢不幸。
I judge from your words that these men also sought the Grail. But I know them not. They have not come to me.	從你的話中，我判斷這些人也在尋找聖杯。但我不識得他們，他們並未來過我這裡。
Hezekiah's Aqueduct feeds the Pool of Siloam by bringing it waters from the Spring of Gihon, the same waters I draw upon for my own pool.	希西家水道將基訓泉的水引入西羅亞池，我這池中所用的，正是同一水源。
The catacombs lie beneath the city. You must find the hierophant if you wish to enter them.	地下墓窖就在城市之下。你若想進入，必須先找到祭司。
The hierophant will guide you to the catacombs, when you are ready. But first I entreat you to pass my Test of Symbols.	待你準備就緒，祭司會引你前往地下墓窖。但在此之前，我懇請你先通過我的符號考驗。
Unless you pass this test, you will enter the catacombs without the gift of the hierophant.	除非你通過此考驗，否則你進入墓窖時，將沒有祭司的贈禮相伴。
Ancient he is, and he is wise, yet shunned by fools who fear his guise. 	他年邁而智慧，卻遭懼其外貌的愚人所棄。 
You have seen the leprous beggar. Look to your own knowledge.	你已見過那染上痲瘋的乞丐。回想你自己所知便是。
The crescent above my inner door signifies that behind it lies the Test of Symbols.	我內門上方的新月，標誌著門後便是符號考驗。
You will learn about that from the hierophant, if ever you meet him.	若你有幸遇見祭司，自會從他那裡得知此事。
She who I serve has infinite names. Yet in all times and in all places she is known by her three natures.	我所侍奉的她擁有無數的名字。然而不論何時何地，她皆以三種神性為人所知。
As the White Virgin she renews and generates life, as the Red Mother she nurtures and protects life, as the Black Crone she is death and the forces of destruction.	化身白色處女時，她更新並創造生命；化身紅色聖母時，她滋養並守護生命；化身黑色老太婆時，她便是死亡與毀滅之力。
You have three more Guardians to face.	你還有三位守護者要面對。
Some questions are more worthy of my answers than others. This one is less worthy.	有些問題比其他問題更值得我回答，這一個不值得。
You shall not move until my dance is through. No other words but a yes or a no will do.	在我的舞蹈結束之前，你不得挪動半步。除了「是」與「否」，其餘言語一概無用。
O' handsome stranger from a distant land, this is my dance of love. I offer you pleasures such as you have never known.	喔，來自遠方的俊美陌生人，這是我的愛之舞。我要獻給你前所未有的歡愉。
I offer you my body and soul and sensual delights beyond imagining. In this enchanted place, we will take our endless fill of one another.	我獻上我的肉身與靈魂，以及超乎想像的感官歡愉。在這方施了魔法的所在，你我將無盡地享受彼此。
I offer you the sweetest wine and the most succulent fruits and meats. I offer you complete freedom from all weariness and care.	我獻上最甘美的酒、最鮮美的果肉，並讓你從一切疲憊與憂慮中徹底解脫。
Kiss me and I will give you forgetfulness and bliss in an earthly paradise. All the pains of your heart and soul will be cured.	吻我，我便賜你忘卻與極樂，如置身人間樂園。你心靈與靈魂的一切傷痛，都將痊癒。
Will you kiss me and be my cherished lover?	你願吻我，做我珍愛的戀人嗎？
Then if the delights of the flesh are not enough for you, I can offer more powerful gifts, for I serve the Goddess herself and I have drunk from her sacred cup.	那麼，若肉體的歡愉還不足以打動你，我能獻上更強大的贈禮——因為我侍奉的正是女神本身，我曾親飲她的聖杯。
Behold!  A vision of the Holy Grail!	且看！聖杯的異象！
I have the power to give you immortality! With but one kiss, you will become invincible. No man, woman or beast will ever overcome you.	我有能力賜你不朽！只消一吻，你便無敵於天下，無論男女或野獸都再也無法勝過你。
You will stride the earth, powerful and invincible, for all time. Think of the deeds of valor you could perform! 	你將以無敵之力縱橫天下，直到永遠。想想你能成就多少英勇的偉業！ 
Will you kiss me and become a god in human form?	你願吻我，化身為人形之神嗎？
Then I find you worthy, King Arthur, and will help you to find what you seek.	那麼，我認定你堪當此任，亞瑟王，我將助你尋得所求之物。
Ask of me what you will.	有話儘管問。
The Street of David ends here against this sacred wall. A beggar sits, coaxing what warmth he can from a brazier filled with burning charcoal.	大衛街到此為止，抵著這面聖牆。一名乞丐坐在此處，就著一只燒著炭火的火盆，勉強取暖。
Though this wall looks to be made of similar stone to the rest of Jerusalem, it is a remnant of a very ancient temple built by King David many hundreds of years ago and is held sacred by the Jewish people.	這面牆的石材看似與耶路撒冷其他建築相仿，實則是數百年前大衛王所建古老聖殿的遺跡，猶太人視之為聖物。
What is this mindless violence that inflicts you? Even a leper has a right to live.	這般不明所以的暴行，是誰加諸於你？即便是痲瘋病人，也有活下去的權利。
Touch a man with leprosy? Do not be a fool!	觸碰一個染上痲瘋的人？別犯傻了！
That would be extraordinarily cruel, Arthur.	那樣做未免太過殘忍了，亞瑟。
A small pile of charcoal burns inside a simple bronze brazier.	一只簡樸的青銅火盆裡，燃著一小堆炭火。
The beggar is a pathetic sight for his limbs are rotting with the disease of leprosy.	這乞丐景況淒慘，四肢正因痲瘋病而腐爛。
The beggar holds a staff in one hand.	這乞丐一手拄著一根拐杖。
A thousand blessings upon for bringing me this charcoal.	承蒙你送來這些炭火，願千般祝福降臨於你。
At night, I suffer from the cold. I have only this brazier in which to burn charcoal, my only source of warmth. Men fear to come near me and I can no longer walk upon my rotted limbs.	入夜之後，我飽受寒冷之苦。我只有這只火盆能燒炭取暖，是我僅有的暖源。人們懼怕靠近我，我這雙腐爛的腿，也再也無法行走。
I must rely upon the goodness of strangers, such as yourself, to bring me charcoal so I will not suffer in the night.	我只能仰賴像你這樣的陌生人心懷善意，為我送來炭火，好讓我夜裡不致受苦。
A small bag of charcoal would be a gift greater than silver or gold to this poor leper.	對這可憐的痲瘋病人而言，一小袋炭火，勝過金銀之贈。
Alms for a poor leper. Look upon the wretched with mercy. Alms for a poor leper.	可憐可憐這痲瘋病人吧。求你以慈悲眼光看待這不幸之人。可憐可憐這痲瘋病人吧。
Sa'alam aleikem, King Arthur. You have passed many trials, yet more Guardians of the Sacred Cup wait to test you.	Sa'alam aleikem，亞瑟王。你已通過重重考驗，但更多聖杯的守護者仍等著試煉你。
